OL,3,GNEWSAO'Neill faces criticism as
OL,4,Anationalist first ministers sign
OL,5,Aagreement
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe deputy first minister has accused
OL,8,Frepublicanism of attempting to
OL,9,F"weaponise the role of the first
OL,10,Fminister", as Michelle O'Neill met the
OL,11,Ffirst ministers of Wales and Scotland
OL,12,Fto discuss ways of "working more
OL,13,Fclosely".
OL,15,FO'Neill, Sinn Fein leader Mary Lou
OL,16,FMcDonald, SNP leader John Swinney and
OL,17,FPlaid Cymru leader Rhun ap Iorwerth are
OL,18,Fcurrently meeting in Cardiff.
OL,20,FThe group met in their capacity as
OL,21,Fparty leaders, rather than as officials
OL,22,Fin their respective governments.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,416,410,260,120,0,100
